  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222128_FY24 #8_WFP_Bangladesh_Nutrition in cox&apos;s Bazaar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- response faces a significant funding deficit in delivering life-saving humanitarian services. The increased match fund is essential to fill this gap, ensuring timely and adequate support reaches the affected population.
 
 - Rebuilding Vital Partnerships, specifically with WFP Nutrition Sector: The discontinuation of our partnership with the WFP nutrition sector in 2021 has resulted in a gap in delivering essential nutritional assistance. Increasing the match fund demonstrates our commitment to reinstating this partnership, vital for comprehensive support to those in need.
 
 - Competitive Landscape and Uniqueness of International Agency Involvement: Local partners offer services at lower costs, but as the sole international agency implementing the grant, our position is unique. Without a substantial match fund contribution, our ability to compete and effectively execute the project diminishes, impacting the aid delivery to the Rohingya crisis.
 
 
 Urgency in Maintaining WFP Presence and Momentum: The sustained presence and momentum of the WFP in providing life-saving nutrition assistance within the Rohingya crisis are paramount. Increasing the match fund aligns directly with preserving WFP&apos;s crucial role in this humanitarian effort.</narrative>
  </description>
